When $\mathbb{F} = \mathbb{Q}$, we have $r_1=1, r_2=0, D=1, d=1, \mathtt{a}_{\mathbb{F}}(n) = 1$ and $H_\mathbb{F} = 1$. We also use \eqref{Z value real} and then \eqref{Exp fn formula} to obtain
\begin{align*}
\tilde{Z}_{r_1, r_2}\left(\frac{2^{r_2}\pi^{d/2} nx}{\sqrt{D}} \right) = 2V(\pi n^2 x^2|0) = 2e^{- n^2\pi x^2}
\end{align*}
Using these values in Corollary \ref{Case k=1 mt2}, we prove Corollary \ref{F=Q, k=1}.

