For $k=2$, the term $R^{(k)}_1(x)$ in Theorem \ref{Theorem Number field analogue Id 2nd paper} reduces to
\begin{align*}
R^{(2)}_1(x) &= \lim_{s\to 1}\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}s}\left((s-1)^2\Omega_\mathbb{F}^2(s)x^{s} \right).
\end{align*}
To solve the above term, we use \eqref{exp series} and \eqref{Laurent series for Omega at s=1} to find the Laurent series expansion of $\Omega_\mathbb{F}^2(s)x^s$ around 1 to have
\begin{align}
&(s-1)^2\Omega_{\mathbb F}^2(s)x^s \notag \\
&= \frac{D H_{\mathbb F}^2 x}{(2\pi)^{2r_2}}
\bigg[ 1+\bigg\{ 2\gamma_{\mathbb F} +\log\left(\frac{Dx}{\pi^d}\right) -d\gamma -2(r_1+r_2)\log 2 \bigg\}(s-1) +O\left((s-1)^2\right) \bigg].\notag
\end{align}
In particular,
\begin{align*}
R^{(2)}_1(x) &= \frac{D H_{\mathbb F}^2x}{(2\pi)^{2r_2}} \left[ 2\gamma_{\mathbb F} +\log\left(\frac{Dx}{\pi^d}\right) -d\gamma -2(r_1+r_2)\log 2\right].
\end{align*}
Upon inserting the above expression for $R^{(2)}_1(x)$ into \eqref{Extended trans formula} and taking $k=2$ in Theorem \ref{Theorem Number field analogue Id 2nd paper}, we obtain Corollary \ref{Gen Koshliakov Formula}.
